       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 600 mg once daily is three times the maximum labeled sertraline dose for adults, which is 200 mg/day. At that dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and severe GI or bleeding effects. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nWas this a typo or a unit mix-up? Here are the usual adult dosing ranges:\n- **Depression, OCD:** Start at 50 mg once daily. Titrate by 25\u201350 mg at intervals of at least one week. The maximum is 200 mg/day.\n- **Panic disorder, PTSD, social anxiety disorder:** Start at 25 mg once daily. Increase to 50 mg after one week, then titrate as needed. The maximum is 200 mg/day.\n\nTell me the intended dose and indication, and I'll enter it. For example, I could enter 50 mg by mouth once daily. Please also confirm it with your resident or attending, and with pharmacy if you want a second check.\n\nIf you really do intend a dose above 200 mg/day, which would be highly unusual, that needs to be discussed with your supervising physician first. I'd also want that decision documented in the order note."
